## Configuration

### Custom Transport Options

```csharp file
using {{packageName}};
using {{packageName}}.Auth;

public static class Transport
{
    public static global::{{packageName}}.{{clientClassName}} ClientWithTransport(IAuthenticator authenticator)
    {
        var transport = TransportOptions.Builder()
            .Proxy("http://proxy:3128")
            .Timeout(5000)
            .Build();

        return new global::{{packageName}}.{{clientClassName}}(authenticator, transport);
    }
}
```

The client implements `IDisposable`. Use `using` statements or call `Dispose()` when done. Streams that are still open are cancelled.

### Retries

`TransportOptions.Builder().MaxRetries(n)` sets the automatic retries (default 2, `0` disables). Retried: a network error before a response and the statuses 408, 409, 429 and 500-599 except 501, after a 0.5 s backoff doubling to 8 s with 25% jitter or the server's `Retry-After` (at most 60 s). The retries never extend the timeout, rebuild the headers on every attempt, and skip single-use and multipart bodies. A 401 on an OAuth2 or OpenID Connect call drops the cached access token and replays the request once (`InvalidateAccessToken()` on those authenticators does the same by hand).

### Per-call options

Every operation takes an optional options object (`<Operation>Options`) that also carries `Timeout` (milliseconds), `MaxRetries` and `Headers` for that call only; null keeps the transport's setting, and an operation with no parameters and no security has an options object with just these three. `Client.FromEnvironment()` builds a bearer client from `{{envVarPrefix}}_HOST` and `{{envVarPrefix}}_TOKEN` (explicit arguments win, a `tokenProvider` callback replaces the token).

### Hooks and telemetry

One optional hook runs around every call: `{{clientClassName}}.WithToken(host, token, callHook: hook)` (or `Configuration.Builder().CallHook(hook)`). `ICallHook.Start(info, headers)` runs once per call after the headers are final and may edit them; it returns an `ICallObserver` (or `null`) whose `Finish(outcome)` runs exactly once with the status (`0` when no response arrived), the lower-cased headers (`null` when none arrived) and the error. An error from `Start` reaches the caller; an error from `Finish` is swallowed. `ICallHook.Chain(a, b)` starts in order and finishes in reverse. `new OpenTelemetryCallHook()` records one span, `http.client.request.count` and `http.client.request.duration` per call; it needs no package, only `AddSource` and `AddMeter` for `{{packageName}}`.

### Credentials from the environment

Each per-scheme authenticator takes optional credential arguments. A value you pass wins, else the environment variable is read once in the constructor (an empty value counts as unset), and a missing credential throws `InvalidOperationException` naming the variable. A bearer authenticator also accepts a `tokenProvider` callback, which wins over the environment.
